{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00135",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 5.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.19,
      "end_seconds": 9.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.27,
      "end_seconds": 15.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Honestly, it's my heart racing, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.17,
      "end_seconds": 18.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.24,
      "end_seconds": 23.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "It's been two weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.3,
      "end_seconds": 32.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.91,
      "end_seconds": 40.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "It just comes and goes. About a four out of ten. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.55,
      "end_seconds": 44.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.85,
      "end_seconds": 60.89,
      "duration_seconds": 15.04,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get lightheadedness as well. Oh, and a fluttering in the chest. That's been about the same, about a week. About fluttering in the chest, a eight out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.73,
      "end_seconds": 64.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.1,
      "end_seconds": 67.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.08,
      "end_seconds": 70.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Have you had any fainting or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.93,
      "end_seconds": 74.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "No, no fainting or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.93,
      "end_seconds": 78.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Have you had any fever, chest pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.2,
      "end_seconds": 83.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "No fever, chest pain or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.33,
      "end_seconds": 96.65,
      "duration_seconds": 12.32,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.71,
      "end_seconds": 100.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 101.86,
      "end_seconds": 113.01,
      "duration_seconds": 11.15,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Heart rate 120, weight 60 kilos. Blood pressure 123 over 78, temperature is 37.0 degrees, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, height 167 centimetres, respiratory rate 20."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.9,
      "end_seconds": 114.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.87,
      "end_seconds": 120.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Bear with me, I need to finish this line in the notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.48,
      "end_seconds": 137.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Alright, back to you. Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.03,
      "end_seconds": 141.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "I've got an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.63,
      "end_seconds": 149.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Yes, I can see the an underactive thyroid in your file as well. Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.92,
      "end_seconds": 152.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.41,
      "end_seconds": 157.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.76,
      "end_seconds": 163.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Right, I'm on thyroxine, 75 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.59,
      "end_seconds": 168.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.99,
      "end_seconds": 169.69,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.26,
      "end_seconds": 184.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.57,
      "end_seconds": 187.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "My mother had high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.43,
      "end_seconds": 193.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "So, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.4,
      "end_seconds": 197.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Yes, pollen, it gives me sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.48,
      "end_seconds": 216.85,
      "duration_seconds": 16.37,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.37,
      "end_seconds": 221.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.52,
      "end_seconds": 223.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Okay, any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.11,
      "end_seconds": 233.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "Just my tonsils out, when I was a child. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.3,
      "end_seconds": 238.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.91,
      "end_seconds": 241.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.18,
      "end_seconds": 257.84,
      "duration_seconds": 15.66,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.7,
      "end_seconds": 260.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.48,
      "end_seconds": 277.69,
      "duration_seconds": 16.21,
      "text": "So, based on your history, my working impression is a possible heart rhythm problem like atrial fibrillation. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together. It could also be anxiety-related palpitations, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.02,
      "end_seconds": 284.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "I mean, I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.74,
      "end_seconds": 300.27,
      "duration_seconds": 14.53,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a possible heart rhythm problem like atrial fibrillation do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had your heart racing for two weeks, and no weight loss or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.93,
      "end_seconds": 303.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.98,
      "end_seconds": 307.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.95,
      "end_seconds": 308.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.29,
      "end_seconds": 324.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Let's get a thyroid test, for palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.21,
      "end_seconds": 326.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.14,
      "end_seconds": 352.88,
      "duration_seconds": 25.74,
      "text": "Let's use metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. That should help with palpitations. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Cut back on tea, coffee and energy drinks, and note the time whenever it happens. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Please don't sit on it if you faint or have chest pain with the racing. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.96,
      "end_seconds": 355.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Come back in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.99,
      "end_seconds": 360.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.31,
      "end_seconds": 369.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.86,
      "end_seconds": 378.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "So, I take the metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.92,
      "end_seconds": 384.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.65,
      "end_seconds": 388.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.55,
      "end_seconds": 390.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}